{
  "extends": "apx-resolution",
  "name": "apx-site-config",
  "description": "The cast of docs/scenarios/by-module/apx-site-config: Lakeside Garage described from APX alone. Exit lane 2 with its barrier, pay-in-lane terminal (the exit verifier), the intercom built into it and the overhead camera; the ground-floor lobby door with its card reader, call-box intercom and ceiling camera; the P1 pay-on-foot station; the P2 ramp camera that still speaks RTSP; the NVR in the equipment room. The comms points a call reaches help through, the PARCS and call-platform ids the garage is known by, the escalation roles, and the after-hours ticket and permit the lobby door scenarios turn on. The exit and entrance signs of lanes 2 and 1 (laneDisplay) with the messages they recorded showing (Part 26 §26.9), the displayMessage command the exit sign once ran, and the stay the unpaid-exit message was for, scored by the compliance engine (Part 5 §5.9).",
